// e2e keeps its own workspace, deliberately separate from the root go.work.
//
// Its test framework (runlog) pins an older google.golang.org/adk whose telemetry
// does not compile against the otel/log version the server's adk/v2 pulls, so
// sharing the root build list would let a server ADK bump break e2e. CI runs
// these modules with GOWORK=off; this file is what keeps a bare `go build ./...` /
// `go test ./...` inside e2e working locally.
//
// The e2e module SHALL stay isolated from the workspace build list. Modules
// listed here are exempt from the root
// coverage guard (.github/scripts/check-go-work-coverage.sh) because they are
// covered by this workspace instead.
go 1.25.6

use (
	.
	./stubs/github
	./stubs/mailgun
	./stubs/mcp-registry
	./stubs/web
)
